天哪，这意味着我们可以听到他的声音了，因为这个男人就算给我读电话

155
00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:52.160
book to me.
簿我也愿意听。

156
00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:53.440
I love his voice.
我爱他的声音。

157
00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.100
I don't know him at all, but I love his voice.
我根本不认识他，但我爱他的声音。

158
00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.820
His voice is in my house all the time because of the Lego movie.
因为《乐高大电影》，他的声音一直在我家里回荡。

159
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.100
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

160
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:06.640
And incidentally, Lego Masters was like our first big family show that helped us get through
顺便说一句，《乐高大师》是我们家第一部帮助我们度过

161
00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:07.580
the beginning of the pandemic.
疫情初期的大型家庭节目。

162
00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.960
You guys love that show.
你们很喜欢那个节目。

163
00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:09.640
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

164
00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.060
All right.
好吧。

165
00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.860
Here is what Will had to say about coming on our show.
这是威尔关于来我们节目做客时说的话。

166
00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:25.380
I remember getting a call, I guess, from my agent saying that Paul Lieberstein from The
我记得接到过经纪人的电话，我想是说《办公室》的保罗·利伯斯坦，

167
00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:30.960
Office, who is obviously the showrunner and one of the stars of the show, wanted to talk
他显然是该剧的剧集主管也是主演之一，想找我谈谈

168
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.240
to me about a role.
一个角色。

169
00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:38.920
I knew that they were looking for a new boss on the show, the character of the boss.
我知道他们当时正在为剧集寻找一位新老板，就是老板那个角色。

170
00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:46.340
So we had a conversation or two and he'd said, hey, we've got this idea and would you want to come
所以我们谈了一两次，他说，嘿，我们有个想法，你想来

171
00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:46.860
and do it?
试试吗？

172
00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:53.460
And I also remember him saying basically to the effect, something to the effect of if it works
我还记得他基本上是这么说的，大意是如果效果好，

173
00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:58.840
out, would you be interested in doing it kind of long-term joining the cast?
你是否有兴趣长期加入剧组？

174
00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.620
And I was a fan of the show.
我当时就是这部剧的粉丝。

175
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:07.900
And of course, I knew a bunch of people on the show and thought, yeah, it would be great.
当然，我也认识剧组里的一群人，觉得，太棒了。

176
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:14.160
And so we talked a few times and it was kind of left like, well, just come and do this episode.
所以我们谈了几次，最后的结果就是，好吧，先来拍这一集。

177
00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:18.080
Just come do this scene and then let's see how it goes.
先来拍这场戏，然后再看看情况如何。

178
00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.900
And I was like, great.
我当时就说，太好了。

179
00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:26.940
At that same time, I was also talking to NBC, the network, about doing a pilot that
与此同时，我也在和NBC电视台谈一部试播集，

180
00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:32.640
Lorne Michaels was producing, written by my friend Emily Spivey with Christina Applegate.
由洛恩·迈克尔斯制作，我朋友艾米丽·斯派维编剧，克里斯蒂娜·艾伯盖特主演。

181
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.200
And it was a great pilot.
那是一部很棒的试播集。

182
00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:39.040
And I just remember that they were both kind of happening around the same time.
我只记得这两件事几乎是同时发生的。

183
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:44.600
So there was a question as to whether or not I could actually do The Office, even if I wanted
所以问题在于，即使我想长期出演《办公室》，我是否真的能做到，

184
00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:49.360
to kind of longer term, even though they hadn't actually said that they wanted me to do that.
尽管他们当时还没明确说希望我长期出演。

185
00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:55.620
But I do remember them kind of both coming around the same time and talking about actually
但我确实记得这两件事几乎同时找上门，我甚至在去拍《办公室》的路上

186
00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:02.620
doing Up All Night on my way to shoot The Office.
还在谈《整夜难眠》的事。

187
00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.180
So anyway, I was a little confused as to what it was going to be.
总之，我当时有点困惑，不知道最后会变成什么样。

188
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:13.420
So I remember all that because I remember he did end up doing that show with Christina Applegate.
所以我记得这一切，因为我记得他最终确实去拍了克里斯蒂娜·艾伯盖特的那部剧。

189
00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:14.200
It's really funny.
那部剧真的很有趣。

190
00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:14.640
Yeah.
是啊。

191
00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.280
And I remember being super bummed because, you know, he and John Krasinski are really
我记得当时特别沮丧，因为，你知道，他和约翰·卡拉辛斯基是

192
00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:19.920
close buddies.
非常要好的朋友。

193
00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.860
And I had worked with him before.
而且我之前也和他合作过。

194
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.640
And John and I were campaigning heavily for Will to join The Office.
我和约翰当时极力游说威尔加入《办公室》。

195
00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.200
To be the new branch manager?
去当新的分部经理吗？

196
00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.880
Or just come on our show.
或者只是来我们的节目。

197
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:29.100
Right, right.
对，没错。

198
00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.860
We just like him so much.
我们就是太喜欢他了。

199
00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:31.160
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

200
00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.580
He's such a good guy.
他真是个好人。

201
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.800
And we wanted him to be on the show so badly.
我们当时特别希望他能来参加节目。

202
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.740
And then he ended up doing that other show.
结果他最后去拍了另一部剧。

203
00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:38.560
Aw.
啊。

204
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.120
I know.
我知道。

205
00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.400
Well, at least he got to come play one day.
好吧，至少他还是来客串了一天。

206
00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:41.120
He did.
确实。

207
00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.980
And I did ask him what was it like to be on the set and doing that scene.
我问过他，在片场拍那场戏是什么感觉。

208
00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.980
And here is what he said.
他是这么说的。

209
00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.940
You come onto a show, especially a show like The Office, that was really good.
当你来到一个剧组，尤其是像《办公室》这样非常出色的剧组时。

210
00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.500
And everybody was, you know, at the top of their game.
每个人都处于最佳状态。

211
00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:56.140
And you just don't want to stand out and be terrible.
你就是不想显得格格不入，表现得太差劲。

212
00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:02.560
And you want to make sure that you're not, you know, coming in at a different volume from
你得确保自己的表演节奏不会和别人。

213
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.460
everybody else.
不在一个频道上。

214
00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:09.520
But I was really excited because I was doing a scene with John Krasinski, who was and still
但我当时真的很兴奋，因为我要和约翰·卡拉辛斯基演对手戏，他当时是，现在也依然。

215
00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:10.700
is one of my good friends.
是我很好的朋友之一。

216
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.720
And that was exciting and fun.
那真的很让人兴奋，也很有趣。

217
00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.820
And then with Paul Lieberstein and Zach Woods.
还有保罗·李伯斯坦和扎克·伍兹。

218
00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.280
And we didn't really talk too much about what it was going to be.
我们并没有过多讨论那场戏会是什么样。

219
00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.440
It was just kind of I'd read the scene.
我只是读了剧本。

220
00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:25.620
And then, you know, we just they're like, all right, they're ready.
然后，你知道，他们就说，好了，准备好了。

221
00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.080
Let's go.
我们开始吧。

222
00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:26.900
And we just started.
我们就直接开始了。

223
00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.180
We just shot it.
直接开拍。

224
00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:30.500
And it was pretty quick.
过程挺快的。

225
00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.500
My memory was that it was kind of over before I knew it.
我的记忆里，还没反应过来就结束了。

226
00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.800
And how long am I supposed to talk for?
我还要说多久？

227
00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:42.080
Is this am I just like 30 minutes?
我是要说30分钟吗？

228
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.760
I was born in Toronto.
我出生在多伦多。

229
00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:46.740
I'm a Taurus.
我是金牛座。

230
00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:54.010
I remember it felt like it was over before it started, too.
我记得当时也觉得还没开始就结束了。

231
00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.310
Well, if you guys love Will Arnett the way we do, go to the DVDs.
好吧，如果你们像我们一样喜欢威尔·阿奈特，那就去看DVD吧。

232
00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:01.030
There is an extended producer's cut for this episode.
这一集有加长版的制片人剪辑版。

233
00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.390
And his scene has a lot more fun stuff.
他的戏份里还有更多有趣的内容。

234
00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.450
His character has a very funny story about being in the Navy.
他的角色有一个关于在海军服役的非常搞笑的故事。

235
00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.150
So if you like Will Arnett, go to the DVD extras.
所以如果你喜欢威尔·阿奈特，去看看DVD花絮吧。

236
00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:11.310
All right.
好的。

237
00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.490
Fast fact number three.
冷知识第三条。

238
00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:16.670
We've talked about all the people from outside of Dunder Mifflin who are applying for this job.
我们聊过所有来自邓德·米夫林公司外部的应聘者。

239
00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.670
But there are three internal applicants.
但其实还有三位内部申请人。

240
00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:22.730
They are Daryl Philbin, Andy Bernard and Dwight Schrute.
他们是达里尔·菲尔宾、安迪·伯纳德和德怀特·舒鲁特。

241
00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:27.210
And after this episode aired, NBC.com posted their resumes.
这一集播出后，NBC.com发布了他们的简历。

242
00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.530
Oh, no way.
噢，不会吧。

243
00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.010
Online.
在网上？

244
00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.030
You found them?
你找到了？

245
00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:30.750
Yes.
是的。

246
00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:32.930
OfficeTelly.com still has them.
OfficeTelly.com上还有。

247
00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:36.450
And I thought I'd read a little bit from each of their resumes.
我想读一下他们各自简历里的一些内容。

248
00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.250
Let's start with Daryl.
先从达里尔开始。

249
00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.710
This is sort of alluded to in the episode.
剧中对此有所暗示。

250
00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.490
You know, Joe is going to say, why is your resume so long?
你知道，乔会问，为什么你的简历这么长？

251
00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:50.410
Aren't you the same Daryl Philbin that has only had two jobs at the same company?
你难道不是那个在同一家公司只做过两份工作的达里尔·菲尔宾吗？

252
00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.550
His resume is four pages long.
他的简历有四页长。

253
00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:53.050
Yes.
是的。

254
00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:59.490
Well, his resume does confirm that Daryl has only ever worked at Dunder Mifflin and it lists
嗯，他的简历确实证实了达里尔只在邓德·米夫林工作过，上面写着

255
00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.930
his starting date as June 1999.
他的入职日期是1999年6月。

256
00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.930
Under work experience, he has a line that says, quote,
在工作经历一栏，他写了一行字，引用如下：

257
00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.710
quote, upheld the highest standard of safety amid the warehouse.
“在仓库中保持了最高安全标准。”

258
00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:16.410
The D'Angelo Vickers incident was the first happening of coma and will not result ever again.
迪安杰洛·维克斯事件是导致昏迷的首例，绝不会再发生。

259
00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:18.250
I can almost promise you that.
我几乎可以向你保证。

260
00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:19.090
End quote.
引用结束。

261
00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:21.650
All right.
好吧。

262
00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:28.230
On Andy's resume, something I found very charming is that the font for Cornell University is larger
在安迪的简历上，我发现一个非常迷人的地方，就是康奈尔大学的字体比

263
00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:32.370
than any other font on the entire page, including the one for his name.
整页纸上任何其他字体都要大，甚至包括他名字的字体。

264
00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:33.210
That tracks.
这很符合他的风格。

265
00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.750
It is also in bold and all caps.
而且还是加粗和大写。

266
00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:41.930
It looks like Andy worked, quote, brief, stressful, yet invaluable, invaluable?
看起来安迪的工作经历写着，引用，“短暂、有压力但无价，无价？”

267
00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:43.210
Invaluable.
无价。

268
00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:43.870
Okay.
好的。

269
00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:51.350
Stints at AIG, Bears, Stearns, Enron, and Lehman Brothers between 1996 and 1998.
1996年到1998年间在AIG、贝尔斯登、安然和雷曼兄弟的短暂工作经历。

270
00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:56.530
And then in 1909, he started working at Dunder Mifflin, Stanford.
然后他在1909年开始在邓德·米夫林斯坦福分公司工作。

271
00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:01.990
And under his special skills, he, of course, lists frolf and banjo.
而在他的特殊技能一栏，他当然列出了飞盘高尔夫和班卓琴。

272
00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:07.130
I'm surprised he hasn't mentioned his summer studying to be a fromage.
我很惊讶他没提到他夏天去学做奶酪师的事。

273
00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.790
I know, the fromagier.
我知道，奶酪师。

274
00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:09.870
Yeah, fromagier.
对，奶酪师。

275
00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.030
Finally, Dwight Kurt Schrute III.
最后，德怀特·库尔特·施鲁特三世。

276
00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.690
Did we know he was a the third?
我们知道他是三世吗？

277
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.990
I feel like somewhere he said he was Dwight K.
我感觉他在什么地方说过他是德怀特·K。

278
00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:20.490
Schrute III.
施鲁特三世。

279
00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.630
I feel like that.
我有这种感觉。

280
00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:22.410
Maybe.
也许吧。

281
00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.530
I have no memory of it.
我完全没印象。

282
00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:23.730
Okay.
好吧。

283
00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.690
But it is listed on his resume.
但简历上确实是这么写的。

284
00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:25.990
Okay.
好吧。

285
00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:33.250
He lists his titles as assistant regional manager, manager slash sales representative,
他列出的头衔是助理区域经理、经理兼销售代表、

286
00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:38.490
beet farmer slash volunteer sheriff deputy, and respected capitaliSt.
甜菜农场主兼志愿警长副手，以及受人尊敬的资本家。

287
00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:44.790
According to his resume, he has only ever been employed at Dunder Mifflin, and he started in 1995.
根据他的简历，他只在邓德·米夫林工作过，而且是1995年入职的。

288
00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.410
That's his only job?
那是他唯一的工作？

289
00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:47.910
Yeah.
是的。

290
00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.230
I'm surprised by that.
我很惊讶。

291
00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:49.730
Me too.
我也是。

292
00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:54.490
By the way, his special skills are listed before his professional experience.
顺便说一下，他的特殊技能列在职业经历之前。

293
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.170
And here are his special skills.
这是他的特殊技能。

294
00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:58.910
Wait, they're at the top?
等等，它们在最上面？

295
00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.670
They are first on the resume.
它们在简历的第一位。

296
00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.030
That is beautiful.
这太美妙了。

297
00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:02.450
Right?
对吧？

298
00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.950
That is how I would love every resume to start.
我希望每份简历都能这样开头。

299
00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.370
That is so good.
这太棒了。

300
00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.150
It actually would be kind of nice.
其实那样还挺不错的。

301
00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:08.410
Yeah.
没错。

302
00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:12.810
You really are going to get a sense of the person first, and then you're going to learn
你确实会先去了解这个人，然后再去了解

303
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:13.830
their job experience.
他们的工作经历。

304
00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:14.750
Okay, go.
好，开始吧。

305
00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.730
All right.
好的。

306
00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:48.270
And proficient in pre-industrial and religious German.
而且精通前工业时代德语和宗教德语。

307
00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:55.630
Now, if that resume came across your desk and you read that, I would be dying to meet this person.
现在，如果这份简历摆在你的桌上，你读了之后，我肯定会迫不及待地想见见这个人。

308
