1561
01:08:04.430 --> 01:08:05.170
I'm excited.
我很兴奋。

1562
01:08:05.890 --> 01:08:09.470
Well, we're about to have some interviews with people from the UK.
好了，我们马上要对来自英国的人进行一些采访。

1563
01:08:09.790 --> 01:08:11.230
First up is David Brent.
首先是大卫·布伦特。

1564
01:08:11.470 --> 01:08:12.330
It's over video.
是通过视频进行的。

1565
01:08:12.690 --> 01:08:16.210
He basically says if they're looking for a leader, he's ready.
他基本上是说，如果他们在寻找领导者，他已经准备好了。

1566
01:08:16.410 --> 01:08:17.210
When does he start?
他什么时候开始？

1567
01:08:17.450 --> 01:08:22.430
So Paul Lieberstein reached out to Ricky Gervais about doing an in-person cameo as one of the
保罗·利伯斯坦联系了瑞奇·热维斯，想让他以申请人之一的身份进行现场客串。

1568
01:08:22.430 --> 01:08:22.930
applicants.
申请人。

1569
01:08:23.130 --> 01:08:27.090
And Ricky really wanted to do it, but he was like working on another project at the time
瑞奇真的很想参加，但他当时正在忙另一个项目，

1570
01:08:27.090 --> 01:08:28.250
and he couldn't travel to LA.
无法前往洛杉矶。

1571
01:08:28.590 --> 01:08:33.590
So first he pitched the idea of filming something in the UK.
所以他首先提议在英国拍摄一些东西。

1572
01:08:33.690 --> 01:08:35.090
Like this was very elaborate.
这真的很费心思。

1573
01:08:35.890 --> 01:08:36.970
It was so nice of him, though.
不过他真是太好了。

1574
01:08:37.170 --> 01:08:43.670
He was like, I'll build like your lobby area and then I'll film my side of it.
他说，我可以搭建你们的办公大厅，然后拍摄我那边的部分。

1575
01:08:43.770 --> 01:08:46.430
And maybe he's the last applicant.
也许他就是最后一位申请人。

1576
01:08:46.810 --> 01:08:49.810
And Pam's kind of like shutting down the office for the day.
帕姆当时正准备结束一天的办公室工作。

1577
01:08:49.850 --> 01:08:55.470
And he walks in and then it would cut to me in the United States just sort of saying
他走了进来，然后画面切到在美国的我，说，

1578
01:08:55.470 --> 01:08:57.190
like, sorry, the interviews are over.
抱歉，面试已经结束了。

1579
01:08:57.190 --> 01:08:59.990
And then he could also then have like a talking head.
然后他还可以有一个采访镜头。

1580
01:09:01.270 --> 01:09:07.790
Or he said, I could just film like a video interview and you could use that.
或者他说，我可以录一段视频面试，你们可以用那个。

1581
01:09:08.490 --> 01:09:11.190
And Paul was like, I think that'll work better.
保罗觉得这样效果更好。

1582
01:09:11.370 --> 01:09:15.570
I think, you know, that was to build the lobby and then get all the lighting right and everything.
你知道，要搭建大厅，还要搞定灯光什么的。

1583
01:09:15.670 --> 01:09:17.090
What if it didn't cut together right?
万一剪辑效果不好怎么办？

1584
01:09:17.110 --> 01:09:17.510
Right, right.
对，没错。

1585
01:09:17.510 --> 01:09:18.930
That could be like a little tricky.
那可能会有点棘手。

1586
01:09:19.430 --> 01:09:22.910
So Ricky sent in four options of interviews.
所以瑞奇发来了四个版本的面试视频。

1587
01:09:23.370 --> 01:09:24.630
We picked this one.
我们选了这一段。

1588
01:09:24.850 --> 01:09:29.190
I bet he did that so fast because that character is just so easy for him.
我敢说他完成得很快，因为那个角色对他来说太简单了。

1589
01:09:29.410 --> 01:09:29.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1590
01:09:29.930 --> 01:09:33.490
I mean, I could watch him do 70 interviews as that character.
我是说，我可以看他演70场那个角色的面试。

1591
01:09:34.130 --> 01:09:38.390
The next person from the UK to interview is going to be Nellie Bertram.
下一位来自英国的面试者是奈莉·伯特拉姆。

1592
01:09:38.390 --> 01:09:39.250
Yes.
是的。

1593
01:09:40.150 --> 01:09:42.590
Catherine Tate plays Nellie Bertram.
凯瑟琳·塔特饰演奈莉·伯特拉姆。

1594
01:09:43.090 --> 01:09:45.450
My gosh, she is amazing.
天哪，她太棒了。

1595
01:09:45.910 --> 01:09:47.250
Such a funny comedian.
真是个有趣的喜剧演员。

1596
01:09:47.650 --> 01:09:50.650
Had her own show in the UK, which is so funny.
她在英国有自己的节目，非常搞笑。

1597
01:09:51.070 --> 01:09:52.110
She's hilarious.
她太搞笑了。

1598
01:09:52.430 --> 01:09:55.270
She's another person I could just watch, read the phone book.
她是另一个我光看她读电话簿都能看下去的人。

1599
01:09:55.470 --> 01:09:58.530
I love that I keep referencing a phone book that no one has anymore.
我喜欢我一直提到没人再用的电话簿这一点。

1600
01:09:59.650 --> 01:10:01.550
But Catherine is so talented.
但凯瑟琳真的太有才了。

1601
01:10:01.770 --> 01:10:05.770
You know, in the shooting draft, they had a different version of the scene that as I read it,
你知道吗，在拍摄剧本里，这场戏有个不同的版本，当我读到它时，

1602
01:10:05.850 --> 01:10:06.770
I could hear her voice.
我仿佛能听到她的声音。

1603
01:10:06.890 --> 01:10:07.630
It was so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1604
01:10:07.630 --> 01:10:10.310
And then this scene is hilarious to me.
而且我觉得这场戏特别好笑。

1605
01:10:10.570 --> 01:10:12.450
She just keeps waffling.
她一直在犹豫不决。

1606
01:10:12.610 --> 01:10:15.230
She's like, first, she's like, no cubicles.
她先是说，不要隔间。

1607
01:10:15.410 --> 01:10:16.470
And then they're like, hmm.
然后他们说，嗯。

1608
01:10:16.590 --> 01:10:18.090
And she's like, definitely cubicles.
接着她说，一定要有隔间。

1609
01:10:18.250 --> 01:10:20.050
And then she's like, no, no, no, no cubicles.
然后她又说，不，不，不，不要隔间。

1610
01:10:20.190 --> 01:10:21.250
Everyone just sits on the floor.
每个人都直接坐在地板上。

1611
01:10:22.110 --> 01:10:23.490
Everybody is their own boss.
每个人都是自己的老板。

1612
01:10:23.630 --> 01:10:25.390
No, everybody's somebody's boss.
不，每个人都是某人的老板。

1613
01:10:25.470 --> 01:10:26.990
And she's just going back and forth.
她就这样反反复复。

1614
01:10:27.550 --> 01:10:32.210
So I guess Catherine Tate said yes immediately, like everyone else.
所以我想凯瑟琳·塔特（Catherine Tate）和大家一样，立刻就答应了。

1615
01:10:32.330 --> 01:10:35.970
But she was in rehearsals for a play when this was shooting.
但拍摄这段戏时，她正在排练一部话剧。

1616
01:10:36.490 --> 01:10:38.910
And she came to do our episode.
她专门赶来拍了我们这一集。

1617
01:10:39.130 --> 01:10:42.630
She was in the United States for like 36 hours.
她在美利坚合众国待了大概36个小时。

1618
01:10:42.890 --> 01:10:43.390
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1619
01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:45.990
She flew in, kind of came directly to set.
她飞过来，算是直接到了片场。

1620
01:10:46.150 --> 01:10:50.250
And then I think she left the very next day because she had to get back for rehearsals.
我想她第二天就走了，因为她得赶回去排练。

1621
01:10:50.250 --> 01:10:51.510
Is that crazy?
这不疯狂吗？

1622
01:10:51.790 --> 01:10:53.110
That is just boss lady.
这才是女强人风范。

1623
01:10:53.790 --> 01:10:57.930
I wanted to read you guys one little thing that was in the shooting draft about the very
我想给你们读一小段拍摄剧本里关于她面试

1624
01:10:57.930 --> 01:10:58.830
end of her interview.
最后的部分。

1625
01:10:59.270 --> 01:11:01.190
It didn't air, but I thought it was very funny.
那段没播出来，但我认为非常有趣。

1626
01:11:01.610 --> 01:11:04.090
She says to Toby, well, what are you offering?
她对托比说，好吧，你提供什么职位？

1627
01:11:04.270 --> 01:11:08.270
And Toby says, well, and before he can finish, she says, right, I'll take it.
托比说，嗯，还没等他说完，她就说，好，我接受。

1628
01:11:08.310 --> 01:11:08.790
Need a job.
需要一份工作。

1629
01:11:08.870 --> 01:11:09.190
Desperate.
走投无路。

1630
01:11:09.290 --> 01:11:09.670
Good match.
绝配。

1631
01:11:09.770 --> 01:11:10.210
Sloppy match.
烂配。

1632
01:11:10.350 --> 01:11:10.510
Whatever.
随便吧。

1633
01:11:11.130 --> 01:11:12.010
Good match.
绝配。

1634
01:11:12.170 --> 01:11:12.930
Sloppy match.
烂配。

1635
01:11:13.130 --> 01:11:13.390
Whatever.
随便吧。

1636
01:11:15.150 --> 01:11:16.170
That's pretty great.
那真是太棒了。

1637
01:11:16.830 --> 01:11:17.110
All right.
好了。

1638
01:11:17.270 --> 01:11:18.410
Final scene of this episode.
这一集的最后一幕。

1639
01:11:18.970 --> 01:11:22.590
Things are going to get real for Jim Halpert.
吉姆·哈珀特（Jim Halpert）要面对现实了。

1640
01:11:22.930 --> 01:11:23.470
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1641
01:11:23.770 --> 01:11:26.390
He's just going to grab a cup of coffee in the kitchen.
他只是去厨房拿杯咖啡。

1642
01:11:26.390 --> 01:11:28.050
And Oscar says, is there a front runner?
奥斯卡（Oscar）问，有热门人选吗？

1643
01:11:28.450 --> 01:11:32.970
And he sort of casually says, well, they're just all sort of blending together after a
他随口说，嗯，过了一会儿，他们看起来都差不多了。

1644
01:11:32.970 --> 01:11:33.270
while.
也许我会直接从帽子里抽个名字出来。

1645
01:11:33.530 --> 01:11:35.450
Maybe I'll just pick a name out of the hat.
噢，那可不太妙。

1646
01:11:35.710 --> 01:11:37.110
Oh, that doesn't go over well.
斯坦利（Stanley）要发飙了。

1647
01:11:37.310 --> 01:11:39.770
Some Stanley sass is about to happen.
他说，你敢。

1648
01:11:39.770 --> 01:11:42.150
He says, the hell you will.
我为上一任老板工作了15年。

1649
01:11:42.350 --> 01:11:45.190
I worked for the last boss for 15 years.
根据我医生的说法，我可没有下一个15年了。

1650
01:11:45.390 --> 01:11:48.010
According to my doctor, I don't have another 15 years.
根据我医生的说法，我可没有下一个15年了。

1651
01:11:48.150 --> 01:11:52.130
If I want to keep up the same dietary and sexual lifestyle, which I intend to.
如果我想保持同样的饮食和性生活方式，而我确实打算这样做的话。

1652
01:11:52.450 --> 01:11:52.970
Yes.
是的。

1653
01:11:53.430 --> 01:11:55.570
My next boss will be my last boss.
我的下一任老板将是我最后一任老板。

1654
01:11:55.910 --> 01:11:57.190
He'll be at my funeral.
他会出席我的葬礼。

1655
01:11:57.930 --> 01:11:58.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1656
01:11:58.630 --> 01:11:59.930
Meredith is ticked off, too.
梅雷迪思也很生气。

1657
01:12:00.150 --> 01:12:03.610
She's like, you pick a crappy boss, you're responsible for my crappy life.
她说，你选了个烂老板，你就得为我这糟糕的生活负责。

1658
01:12:03.750 --> 01:12:05.010
And then Oscar.
还有奥斯卡。

1659
01:12:05.530 --> 01:12:06.370
Oscar's annoyed.
奥斯卡很恼火。

1660
01:12:06.930 --> 01:12:07.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1661
01:12:07.370 --> 01:12:15.510
And then Ryan says, maybe, maybe Jim should take a day off from his gym shtick and try
然后瑞安说，也许，也许吉姆该歇一天，别再搞他那套健身房把戏了，试着

1662
01:12:15.510 --> 01:12:17.410
caring about something for a change.
关心一下别的事情。

1663
01:12:18.110 --> 01:12:18.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1664
01:12:18.470 --> 01:12:21.050
That was my second favorite line in the whole episode.
那是整集里我第二喜欢的台词。

1665
01:12:21.290 --> 01:12:24.970
Little advice, take a day off from the whole gym shtick.
给个小建议，歇一天吧，别再搞那套健身房把戏了。

1666
01:12:25.210 --> 01:12:25.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1667
01:12:25.610 --> 01:12:26.670
And then he calls him James.
然后他叫他詹姆斯。

1668
01:12:26.930 --> 01:12:29.030
And then he shuts his door to his little closet.
接着他关上了他那个小壁橱的门。

1669
01:12:29.830 --> 01:12:35.680
Oh, well, that is the search committee part one.
好吧，这就是“搜寻委员会”第一部分的内容。

1670
01:12:36.020 --> 01:12:39.780
A big thank you to Will Arnett for sending in those audio clips.
非常感谢威尔·阿奈特发来那些音频片段。

1671
01:12:39.960 --> 01:12:45.380
And to Paul Lieberstein, who traded countless texts with me so that I could get all my info
还要感谢保罗·利伯斯坦，他和我交换了无数条短信，让我能把所有信息

1672
01:12:45.380 --> 01:12:45.720
right.
都弄准确。

1673
01:12:45.960 --> 01:12:49.900
And to Creed Bratton for chatting with me on the phone about being the branch manager.
还要感谢克里德·布拉顿在电话里和我聊关于担任分公司经理的事。

1674
01:12:50.320 --> 01:12:52.280
And finally, Randy Cordray.
最后是兰迪·科德雷。

1675
01:12:52.280 --> 01:12:56.080
Guys, these were Randy's last episodes.
伙计们，这些是兰迪参与的最后几集了。

1676
01:12:56.320 --> 01:13:00.240
So we're going to be saying goodbye to Randy after next week.
所以下周之后我们就要和兰迪说再见了。

1677
01:13:00.240 --> 01:13:04.200
And I don't want to stop emailing him every week.
我可不想停止每周给他发邮件。

1678
01:13:04.200 --> 01:13:05.060
I just love it.
我太喜欢这样了。

1679
01:13:05.240 --> 01:13:05.660
I know.
我知道。

1680
01:13:05.860 --> 01:13:08.080
Randy is the most lovely person.
兰迪是个非常可爱的人。

1681
01:13:08.320 --> 01:13:13.800
Not only has he been so gracious with his time and sending us really detailed emails about
他不仅慷慨地抽出时间，给我们发送关于每一集非常详细的邮件，

1682
01:13:13.800 --> 01:13:17.200
each episode, but he's just a wonderful human.
而且他本身就是一个很棒的人。

1683
01:13:17.340 --> 01:13:20.080
And he gives us emails of encouragement.
他还会给我们发鼓励的邮件。

1684
01:13:20.280 --> 01:13:22.060
He lets us know that we're doing it right.
他让我们知道我们做得对。

1685
01:13:22.220 --> 01:13:23.160
He checks in on us.
他会关心我们的近况。

1686
01:13:23.260 --> 01:13:24.780
We just adore him so much.
我们真的非常喜欢他。

1687
01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:28.320
Well, and that's how he was when he was the line producer of our show.
嗯，他在担任我们节目的执行制片人时也是这样。

1688
01:13:28.540 --> 01:13:29.400
Same person.
始终如一。

1689
01:13:30.200 --> 01:13:30.820
All right.
好了。

1690
01:13:30.920 --> 01:13:32.520
Next week, search committee part two.
下周，“搜寻委员会”第二部分。

1691
01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:33.240
See you then.
到时见。

1692
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:34.100
Bye.
再见。

